POSITION
TERMS OF REFERENCE (for job postings)
POSITION TITLE: Program Manager – Tertiary
LOCATION: Port Moresby
REPORTING TO: Head of Tertiary
ABOUT KTF:
KTF is an Australian international aid and development organisation working in Papua New Guinea (PNG).
We work with people and communities to improve the lives and futures of Papua New Guineans. We do this by: assisting remote and rural communities with access to elementary and primary
education
;
improving access to quality and accessible
healthcare
;
improving
equality
and access to sustainable income-generation opportunities, especially for women; and by fostering the next generation of
leaders
.
KTF is a member of the Australian Council for International Development and is accredited with the Department of Foreign Affairs and Trade’s Australian Not-for-Profit Cooperation Program.
ABOUT THE ROLE:
The Program Manager – Tertiary role is a position in Port Moresby created to assist with coordinating KTF’s tertiary projects, which deliver high-quality teaching and active learning, practical work experience, and research to foster critical thinking, and pathways to employment for teachers and health workers in PNG.
The Program Manager – Tertiary position will work closely with KTF’s Head of Tertiary to effectively implement the academic and non-academic activities associated with the operations of tertiary institutions in remote PNG.
RESPONSIBILITIES:
Operational Support to Tertiary Programs
Support day-to-day coordination of Tertiary Programs;
Ensure activities are implemented in line with approved workplans;
Support Principals to resolve operational issues;
Monitor enrolment, attendance, retention, and completion trends;
Identify and escalate operational risks or delivery issues;
Systems, Processes & Compliance
Support annual project management cycles;
Ensure staff records, inventories, and reports are up to date;
Conduct operational spot checks;
Ensure logistics systems are in place and staff coordinate travel, transport and logistics effectively;
Safeguarding, Risk & Cross-Cutting Priorities
Support implementation of safeguarding and inclusion policies;
Monitor safeguarding compliance;
Support incident reporting and follow-up;
Assist with safety and risk management;
Support to Principals
Conduct regular operational check-ins;
Support supervision and performance tracking;
Identify training and development needs;
Act as a communication link between Principals and the Program Manager;
Reporting, Data & Donor Compliance
Ensure donor compliance, reporting requirements and professional standards are maintained across Southern Region FODE Centres;
Collect and validate operational data;
Support donor reporting inputs;
Support donor visits and field logistics;
Ensure donor branding requirements are met.
Stakeholder Engagement
Maintain effective relationships where required with DHERST, NDoE, Provincial Education Offices, and District Education Authorities
Ensure program delivery aligns with DHERST policy and standards
SKILLS & ATTRIBUTES:
Excellent organisational skills
Strong written and verbal communication skills
Strong capability with the use of Google Suite, Microsoft Office, including intermediate document and spreadsheet skills
General level of technology skills (Gmail, Slack, Project Monday, Moodle Workplace)
Strong project coordination and administrative skills, with the ability to plan, organise and monitor project activities
High level of accuracy and attention to detail, particularly in data management, reporting and record keeping
Ability to work independently with minimal supervision while also contributing effectively as part of a team
A tertiary qualification in project management, international development, business administration, education, health, logistics or a related discipline. Or equivalent relevant professional experience.
Applicants must have the right to work in PNG.
This position may require travel domestically from time to time.
